# {{PROJECT_SLUG}}-context

Where the **{{PROJECT_NAME}}** project keeps what is true today — scope, decisions,
vocabulary, ownership — and the Claude Code plugin the whole team shares.

| I want to… | Go to |
| :-- | :-- |
| Understand the idea | [GUIDE.md](GUIDE.md) |
| Find a document or its owner | [docs/README.md](docs/README.md) |
| Check what was decided | [docs/decisions/](docs/decisions/README.md) |
| Look up a term | [docs/glossary.md](docs/glossary.md) |
| Use the knowledge from a code repository | Connect it once with `/tsh-product-management:initializing-project-context` (*Attach repository*), then `/tsh-product-management:navigating-project-context` |
| Change a document | A branch and a pull request — in the git host's web editor, or with `/tsh-product-management:writing-project-knowledge` |
| Check before a pull request | `python3 scripts/check_links.py && python3 scripts/check_tables.py && python3 scripts/check_decisions.py`; the pipeline adds `check_plugin.py`, which compares with the default branch |

